 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 27583,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"36\" data-start=\"0\">The key difference is:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"406\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"38\">\n\t<li data-end=\"207\" data-start=\"38\">\n\t<p data-end=\"207\" data-start=\"40\"><strong data-end=\"65\" data-start=\"40\">Computer Organization</strong> refers to the physical components of a computer system and how they are interconnected (e.g., circuit design, control signals, memory types).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"406\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"208\">\n\t<p data-end=\"406\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"210\"><strong data-end=\"235\" data-start=\"210\">Computer Architecture</strong> refers to the logical structure and behavior of a computer system as seen by the programmer, including elements like instruction sets, addressing modes, and data formats.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>What is the key difference between computer organization and computer architecture?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 101,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 27583
  },
  {
   "_id": 37188,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"36\" data-start=\"0\">Microcomputers are the smallest type of computers designed for individual use. They use microprocessors as the CPU and are cost-effective, portable, and easy to operate. They are widely used in homes, schools, and offices for word processing, browsing, and entertainment. Examples include desktops, laptops, and tablets</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Explain the characteristics of microcomputers with examples.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 101,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 37188
  },
  {
   "_id": 37189,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1804\" data-start=\"1712\">Computers are classified into four categories based on size and performance:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"2217\" data-start=\"1805\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1866\" data-start=\"1805\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1866\" data-start=\"1807\"><strong data-end=\"1825\" data-start=\"1807\">Microcomputers</strong> &ndash; Smallest, designed for personal use.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1933\" data-start=\"1867\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1933\" data-start=\"1869\"><strong data-end=\"1886\" data-start=\"1869\">Minicomputers</strong> &ndash; Medium-sized, used by small organizations.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2019\" data-start=\"1934\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2019\" data-start=\"1936\"><strong data-end=\"1950\" data-start=\"1936\">Mainframes</strong> &ndash; Large, powerful, support hundreds of users, used in enterprises.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2217\" data-start=\"2020\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2217\" data-start=\"2022\"><strong data-end=\"2040\" data-start=\"2022\">Supercomputers</strong> &ndash; Most powerful, used for research and complex simulations.<br data-end=\"2103\" data-start=\"2100\" />\n\tThis classification helps in choosing the right computer system depending on the workload and user requirements.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Write a short note on how computers are classified based on size and performance.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 101,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 37189
  }
