 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 25639,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"460\" data-start=\"273\"><strong data-end=\"286\" data-start=\"273\">Gr</strong><strong data-end=\"286\" data-start=\"273\">ay Code</strong> is a binary numeral system where two successive values differ in only one bit. It is mainly used in analog to digital conversions to prevent errors due to signal transition.</p>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"502\" data-start=\"462\"><strong data-end=\"502\" data-start=\"467\">Binary to Gray Code Conversion:</strong></h4>\n\n<p data-end=\"511\" data-start=\"503\">Steps:</p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"724\" data-start=\"512\">\n\t<li data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"512\">\n\t<p data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"515\">The <strong data-end=\"549\" data-start=\"519\">most significant bit (MSB)</strong> of the Gray code is the same as the MSB of the binary number.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"724\" data-start=\"614\">\n\t<p data-end=\"724\" data-start=\"617\">Each subsequent Gray bit is obtained by <strong data-end=\"664\" data-start=\"657\">XOR</strong>ing the current binary bit with the <strong data-end=\"723\" data-start=\"700\">previous binary bit</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p data-end=\"888\" data-start=\"726\"><strong data-end=\"738\" data-start=\"726\">Example:</strong><br data-end=\"741\" data-start=\"738\" />\nBinary: <code data-end=\"756\" data-start=\"749\">01001</code><br data-end=\"759\" data-start=\"756\" />\nStep 1: MSB = <code data-end=\"776\" data-start=\"773\">0</code><br data-end=\"779\" data-start=\"776\" />\nStep 2: <code data-end=\"798\" data-start=\"787\">1 &oplus; 0 = 1</code><br data-end=\"801\" data-start=\"798\" />\nStep 3: <code data-end=\"820\" data-start=\"809\">0 &oplus; 1 = 1</code><br data-end=\"823\" data-start=\"820\" />\nStep 4: <code data-end=\"842\" data-start=\"831\">0 &oplus; 0 = 0</code><br data-end=\"845\" data-start=\"842\" />\nStep 5: <code data-end=\"864\" data-start=\"853\">1 &oplus; 0 = 1</code><br data-end=\"867\" data-start=\"864\" />\n<strong data-end=\"888\" data-start=\"867\">Gray Code = 01101</strong></p>\n\n<hr data-end=\"893\" data-start=\"890\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"930\" data-start=\"895\"><strong data-end=\"930\" data-start=\"900\">Gray to Binary Conversion:</strong></h4>\n\n<p data-end=\"939\" data-start=\"931\">Steps:</p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"940\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1007\" data-start=\"940\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1007\" data-start=\"943\">The <strong data-end=\"964\" data-start=\"947\">MSB of Binary</strong> is the same as the MSB of the Gray code.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1008\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1057\" data-start=\"1011\">Each next binary bit is obtained as follows:</p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1061\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1138\" data-start=\"1061\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1138\" data-start=\"1063\">If the Gray bit is <code data-end=\"1085\" data-start=\"1082\">0</code>, the binary bit is <strong data-end=\"1136\" data-start=\"1105\">same as previous binary bit</strong></p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1142\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1144\">If the Gray bit is <code data-end=\"1166\" data-start=\"1163\">1</code>, the binary bit is <strong data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1186\">inverse of the previous binary bit</strong></p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p data-end=\"1461\" data-start=\"1226\"><strong data-end=\"1238\" data-start=\"1226\">Example:</strong><br data-end=\"1241\" data-start=\"1238\" />\nGray: <code data-end=\"1254\" data-start=\"1247\">01101</code><br data-end=\"1257\" data-start=\"1254\" />\nStep 1: MSB = <code data-end=\"1274\" data-start=\"1271\">0</code><br data-end=\"1277\" data-start=\"1274\" />\nStep 2: Gray = <code data-end=\"1295\" data-start=\"1292\">1</code> &rarr; invert <code data-end=\"1308\" data-start=\"1305\">0</code> &rarr; <code data-end=\"1314\" data-start=\"1311\">1</code><br data-end=\"1317\" data-start=\"1314\" />\nStep 3: Gray = <code data-end=\"1335\" data-start=\"1332\">1</code> &rarr; invert <code data-end=\"1348\" data-start=\"1345\">1</code> &rarr; <code data-end=\"1354\" data-start=\"1351\">0</code><br data-end=\"1357\" data-start=\"1354\" />\nStep 4: Gray = <code data-end=\"1375\" data-start=\"1372\">0</code> &rarr; same as previous &rarr; <code data-end=\"1400\" data-start=\"1397\">0</code><br data-end=\"1403\" data-start=\"1400\" />\nStep 5: Gray = <code data-end=\"1421\" data-start=\"1418\">1</code> &rarr; invert <code data-end=\"1434\" data-start=\"1431\">0</code> &rarr; <code data-end=\"1440\" data-start=\"1437\">1</code><br data-end=\"1443\" data-start=\"1440\" />\n<strong data-end=\"1461\" data-start=\"1443\">Binary = 01001</strong></p>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1466\" data-start=\"1463\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1468\"><strong data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1473\">Applications:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1596\" data-start=\"1491\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1543\" data-start=\"1491\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1543\" data-start=\"1493\">Minimizing transition errors in digital circuits</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1565\" data-start=\"1544\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1565\" data-start=\"1546\">Position encoders</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1596\" data-start=\"1566\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1596\" data-start=\"1568\">Analog-to-digital converters</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Explain the working of Gray Code. How is Binary to Gray and Gray to Binary conversion done? Illustrate with an example.</p>\n",
